WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.177
Use if and else when exactly one of two outcomes should happen.

00:00:04.177 --> 00:00:06.507
Here sales is seven hundred.

00:00:06.507 --> 00:00:10.552
The condition asks whether sales is greater than eight hundred.

00:00:10.552 --> 00:00:16.292
That is false, so Python skips the if block and runs the else block instead.

00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:20.152
Change sales to nine hundred and run the cell again.

00:00:20.152 --> 00:00:23.112
Now the first branch should run.

00:00:23.112 --> 00:00:31.637
This two-way pattern appears everywhere: pass or fail, valid or invalid, above target or below target,

00:00:31.637 --> 00:00:33.611
approved or not approved.
